  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "De Zille entered single-seater racing with support from the family behind the Lesley Dee fashion company and its First Edition and Harvest Moon brands. Pegasus Motorsport was created around that programme, and he won the BP Superfind Junior Formula Ford title in 1983. He advanced into British Formula Three, driving Ralt machinery as the team developed toward higher categories.\n\nAfter a long interval, de Zille returned to sustained competition in Ferrari’s British one-make series. He won the Coppa Shell championship in 2021 and continued racing Ferrari machinery in later seasons. He also moved into GT events, sharing drives with his son Dan in Ferrari Challenge and GT Cup competition. The later career turned an early family-backed opportunity into a durable personal identity in British club and marque racing.",
    "html": "<p>De Zille entered single-seater racing with support from the family behind the Lesley Dee fashion company and its First Edition and Harvest Moon brands. Pegasus Motorsport was created around that programme, and he won the BP Superfind Junior Formula Ford title in 1983. He advanced into British Formula Three, driving Ralt machinery as the team developed toward higher categories.</p>\r\n<p>After a long interval, de Zille returned to sustained competition in Ferrari’s British one-make series. He won the Coppa Shell championship in 2021 and continued racing Ferrari machinery in later seasons. He also moved into GT events, sharing drives with his son Dan in Ferrari Challenge and GT Cup competition. The later career turned an early family-backed opportunity into a durable personal identity in British club and marque racing.</p>\r\n",
